## [Quick exercise (XI): age in months]{style="color:darkseagreen"}

**Write a function that calculates your approximate age in months.**

Hints:

```{r, echo = TRUE, eval = FALSE, webex.hide = "Hint"}
?as.Date
?difftime
```

A first possible solution is:

```{r, echo = TRUE, error=TRUE, eval = TRUE, webex.hide = "Answer 1"}
# Quick version using Sys.Date() and as.Date().
age <- function(x){
  # Check whether x can be interpreted as a date in YYYY-MM-DD format.
  if (!is.na(as.Date(as.character(x), format="%Y-%m-%d"))){
    # Difference between today and the birth date, in days.
    age <- as.numeric(Sys.Date() - as.Date(x, format="%Y-%m-%d"))

    # Approximate months by dividing by 30.
    print(paste("You are about", round(age/30, 1), "months old"))
  } else {
    stop("The input date must be quoted and in format YYYY-MM-DD")
  }
}

# Test examples.
age(18)
age("2004-11-17")
```

A second possible solution can ask the user for input when the date is missing.

```{r, echo = TRUE, error=TRUE, eval = TRUE, webex.hide = "Answer 2"}
# Alternative using interactive input and difftime().
df <- function(x){
  # If x is missing, ask the user for input.
  # This is interactive, so it is more useful in the console than in a rendered page.
  if (missing(x)){
    x <- readline(prompt="Introduce your birthdate in the format YYYY-MM-DD: ")
  }

  # Check whether x can be interpreted as a date.
  if (!is.na(as.Date(as.character(x), format="%Y-%m-%d"))){
    df <- difftime(Sys.Date(), as.Date(x, format="%Y-%m-%d"))
    print(paste0("If you were born on ", x, ", you are about ", round(as.numeric(df)/30, 1), " months old."))
  } else {
    stop("The input date must be in format YYYY-MM-DD")
  }
}

df("2004-11-17")
df(18)
df()
```

